{
  "$comment": "The extras of omx-keyed-gate's declaration: what its descriptor, omx-keyed-gate.descriptor.json, has no word for (docs/declaration-as-descriptor.md). The two are the folder's hand-written files; tools/gen.mjs generates the rest and writes the travels the descriptor's links resolve to. Its parameters are by reference to omx-contract's gate kernel and bind by name to omx-dsp's instance face. Control order, the descriptor's, is append-only.",
  "stem": "omx-keyed-gate",
  "kernel": "gate",
  "kernels": [
    "gate"
  ],
  "noun": "keyed gate",
  "url": "https://github.com/Open-Mixer/omx-plugins",
  "summary": "The console's channel gate with a sidechain key: the detector listens to the key your host routes to it, or to the signal itself. One gain for both legs, so the stereo image never shifts. Real-time safe.",
  "binding": "instance",
  "held": [
    "keyListen",
    "keyTiltDb"
  ],
  "controls": {
    "key_external": {
      "control": "keySource",
      "values": [
        "Self",
        "Sidechain"
      ],
      "defaultId": "sidechain"
    },
    "key_hp": {
      "control": "hpHz"
    },
    "key_lp": {
      "control": "lpHz"
    }
  },
  "sidechain": {
    "symbol": "key",
    "name": "Key (Sidechain)"
  },
  "portHints": {
    "key": {
      "props": [
        "lv2:connectionOptional",
        "lv2:isSideChain"
      ]
    },
    "enabled": {
      "props": [
        "lv2:toggled"
      ]
    },
    "key_external": {
      "props": [
        "lv2:enumeration",
        "lv2:integer"
      ],
      "points": [
        "0 Self",
        "1 Sidechain"
      ]
    },
    "threshold": {
      "unit": "units:db"
    },
    "ratio": {
      "props": [
        "pprops:logarithmic"
      ]
    },
    "range": {
      "unit": "units:db"
    },
    "attack": {
      "unit": "units:ms"
    },
    "release": {
      "unit": "units:ms"
    },
    "knee_start": {
      "props": [
        "lv2:integer"
      ],
      "unit": "units:db"
    },
    "knee_end": {
      "props": [
        "lv2:integer"
      ],
      "unit": "units:db"
    },
    "hold": {
      "props": [
        "lv2:integer"
      ],
      "unit": "units:ms"
    },
    "hysteresis": {
      "unit": "units:db"
    },
    "key_hp": {
      "props": [
        "lv2:integer"
      ],
      "unit": "units:hz"
    },
    "key_lp": {
      "props": [
        "lv2:integer"
      ],
      "unit": "units:hz"
    },
    "latency": {
      "props": [
        "lv2:integer"
      ],
      "unit": "units:frame"
    }
  },
  "resourceHints": {
    "threads-spawned": 0,
    "streams-from-disk": false,
    "opens-sockets": false
  },
  "meters": [
    {
      "id": "gateGr",
      "kind": "gain_reduction",
      "field": "gate.st.gr_min_db",
      "readout": "GAIN_REDUCTION_DB"
    }
  ],
  "panel": {
    "family": "gate",
    "roles": {
      "threshold": "threshold",
      "range": "range",
      "attack": "attack",
      "release": "release",
      "hold": "hold",
      "knee_start": "knee_start",
      "knee_end": "knee_end",
      "hysteresis": "hysteresis",
      "ratio": "ratio"
    },
    "sections": [
      {
        "key": "gate",
        "label": "Gate",
        "controls": [
          "threshold",
          "range",
          "ratio",
          "attack",
          "hold",
          "release",
          "hysteresis",
          "knee_start",
          "knee_end"
        ],
        "graph": "dynamics-curve"
      },
      {
        "key": "key",
        "label": "Key",
        "controls": [
          "key_external",
          "key_hp",
          "key_lp"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "manual": [
    "The console's gate, keyed: the stereo signal is gated while the detector listens to a second, mono",
    "input, the **key** (an LV2 sidechain port; in CLAP a second input port). With nothing routed to the",
    "key, or **Key** set to Self, it is the ordinary self-keyed gate.",
    "",
    "| Parameter | Range | Default |",
    "|---|---|---|",
    "| Key | {range:key_external} | {default:key_external} |",
    "| Threshold | {range:threshold} | {default:threshold} |",
    "| Ratio | {range:ratio} | {default:ratio} |",
    "| Range | {range:range} | {default:range} |",
    "| Attack | {range:attack} | {default:attack} |",
    "| Release | {range:release} | {default:release} |",
    "| Knee start | {range:knee_start} | {default:knee_start} |",
    "| Knee end | {range:knee_end} | {default:knee_end} |",
    "| Hold | {range:hold} | {default:hold} |",
    "| Hysteresis | {range:hysteresis} | {default:hysteresis} |",
    "| Key high-pass | {range:key_hp} | {default:key_hp} |",
    "| Key low-pass | {range:key_lp} | {default:key_lp} |",
    "",
    "Plus the host's bypass. An attack under 0.5 ms engages the 4x detector path, which adds 72 frames",
    "of latency, reported to the host; otherwise the latency is zero. Its LV2 URI, ports and defaults",
    "are those of the keyed gate bundle the OpenMixer console used to ship, so a session saved with that",
    "bundle loads this one."
  ],
  "console": {
    "$comment": "The OpenMixer console draws its gate stage and its key in the processing strip: the gate's curve beside its encoders (thresholdDb, rangeDb, ratio, attackMs, holdMs, releaseMs, hysteresisDb), the knee as readouts (knee_start, knee_end are not drawn as controls), then the KEY section (key source select, key HP and LP; the voice-band button and listen have no parameter here). Its chip shows the gate's main settings. Its overview card carries the gate's controls.",
    "placement": {
      "group": "walk",
      "stage": "gate",
      "fxGroup": "dynamics"
    },
    "card": {
      "show": [
        "threshold",
        "range",
        "attack",
        "release"
      ]
    },
    "chip": "THR {threshold}"
  }
}
